; Reviewed export-origin exceptions (tools/libraries/origins.scm).
;
; Each entry is (name defining-library ...): NAME is exported with different
; definitions from these libraries, and that is intentional because every
; NAME here is specified by a SRFI or R7RS library with different semantics
; (for example SRFI 13 vs SRFI 125 string-hash, SRFI 140 immutable strings,
; SRFI 44 collection operations over R7RS names).  A program that imports
; two of these libraries gets the compiler's conflict diagnostic.
;
; The gate fails on any overlap not listed here, and on a listed entry that
; no longer conflicts, so this list can only shrink.  A non-standard name is
; never allowed here: rename one of the definitions instead.
